ecause earlier paul had  visions of james being a friend someone  who taught paul about the desert but  because of paul's choices and chance  that vision didn't come true and paul  had to kill the man who could have been  his friend  so paul's visions aren't guaranteed  they're only possibilities like plans  dreams hopes and fears in the real world  they can guide us to achieve our goals  but they can also blind us and limit our  thinking  june explores the power and the danger  of predictions and dreams  in the book paul cries for james and the  fremen see crying as a profound sacred  act because of how precious water is in  the desert paul says that james was his  friend that james taught him that  killing has a price  so maybe in a way paul's vision of james  as a friend who taught him did come true  after all  the fremen wrap up james's body and take  it with them because when a freman dies  the water is drained from their body in  a death still and reclaimed for the  fremen to use  the flesh belongs to the person but his  water belongs to the tribe  in the movie paul gives a confident  heroic speech he says he sees the future  and that he chooses to be with the  fremen but at this point in the book the  vibe is darker and uncertain paul and  jessica are unsure about the freeman but  feel forced to use them to survive paul  doesn't see his future clearly he feels  he is plunged into the abyss he's afraid  of his visions of the bloody jihad and  desperately hopes to prevent it paul's  destiny is dangerous  we see a freeman riding a sand worm to  travel we have much more to learn about  the power of the fremen and their desert  cheyney says this is only the beginning  and it really is  this june movie only covers the first  half of the first book in the dune  trilogy which itself is just the  beginning of a larger series there is so  much more to this story  frank herbert said that the first june  book has a coital rhythm meaning the  pacing of the story is like sex it  starts slow and speeds up and then  suddenly climactically ends  so by ending this movie halfway through  the first book denny villeneuve stops  mid coitus leaving us waiting without a  climax until june part 2 comes out  this movie is a mostly faithful  adaptation of the first half of the  first book it introduces the worlds and  politics of the imperium the mysterious  spacing guild the scheming bene jesuit  the evil harkenans defeat the atreides  paul and jessica escape to the fremen  and they start to learn the ways of the  desert we see paul's complicated destiny  and ambiguous visions with hints of the  dangers of the messiah  the movie introduces ideas of the  environment and religion and political  exploitation and the power of the mind  but the movie leaves out some important  scenes like the dinner party and the  traitor subplot it doesn't capture the  tragedy of dr yui the meaning of kain's  death or the darker manipulative side of  lato and jessica it removes some of the  arabic references from the fremen and it  skips some plotlines with the  hearkenance and with thufia hopefully  we'll get this in the next june movie  but to understand the meaning of paul's  story and the message of dune we've got  to talk about the other books in the  series so we've got another video called  the philosophy of june coming out soon  we've also got a podcast episode out now  talking about tune with quinn from  quinn's ideas we're also doing a q a  live stream about dune on this channel  in 24 hours and for some reason  professional [ __ ] poster alt swift x has  released a rap about june so go check  out all that gian content linked below  we're going to make more dune videos in  the future we're also covering more song  of ice and fire and the upcoming game of  thrones prequel tv show house of the  dragon house of the dragon is based on a  book called fire and blood you can get  fire and blood or dune as an audio book  for free right now at audible.com asx  sign